  "risks": [
    {
      "title": "Dépendance au partenariat de distribution Coca-Cola",
      "category": "strategic",
      "severity": 5,
      "score_rationale": "Item 1A milieu (frac 0.35), risque coeur : 'Coca-Cola Hellenic, Coca-Cola FEMSA...are our primary domestic and international distributors'. Distribution 100% dependante TCCC. Citation: \"In February 2025, the Amended and Restated International Distribution Coordination Agreement with TCCC was renewed\". Position: bas Item 1A.",
      "trend": "stable",
      "summary": "Distribution mondiale repose largement sur le réseau d'embouteilleurs Coca-Cola (TCCC, actionnaire 19,9% post-2014). Toute dégradation de la relation, renégociation des termes ou changement stratégique chez TCCC (focus boissons saines, restructurations embouteilleurs) impacterait la disponibilité produits.",
      "score": 5
    },
    {
      "title": "Régulation boissons énergisantes et taxes santé",
      "category": "regulatory",
      "severity": 3,
      "score_rationale": "Item 1A milieu (frac 0.47), formulation conditionnelle : 'additional cautionary labeling or packaging requirements might be imposed'. Regulation boissons energisantes standard. Citation: \"Distribution Agreements During 2025, we continued to expand distribution of our products in both our\". Position: milieu Item 1A.",
      "trend": "up",
      "summary": "Pression réglementaire croissante : interdictions ventes aux mineurs (UK 2024, Allemagne, Lituanie, Pologne), taxes sucre/caféine (Royaume-Uni Soft Drinks Industry Levy, Mexique IEPS), warnings labels FDA. WHO recommande limitation caféine. Impact volumes et marketing dans plusieurs marchés.",
      "score": 3
    },
    {
      "title": "Concurrence Celsius, Red Bull et nouveaux entrants performance",
      "category": "competitive",
      "severity": 4,
      "score_rationale": "Item 1A milieu (frac 0.50), concurrents nommes : 'CELSIUS, PRIME, C4, Alani Nu, GHOST, ZOA, GORGIE'. Nouveaux entrants performance identifies. Citation: \"From time to time, competitors have entered into distribution or acquisition agreements with certain other\". Position: bas Item 1A.",
      "trend": "up",
      "summary": "Concurrence intense de Red Bull (leader global), Celsius (croissance >100% en 2022-2023, distribution PepsiCo), Bang (acquis par Monster en 2023), Alani Nu, C4 et private labels (Rockstar, store brands). Parts de marché Monster aux US sous pression. Acquisition Bang Energy pour défendre le segment performance.",
      "score": 4
    },
    {
      "title": "Volatilité matières premières (aluminium, sucre, caféine)",
      "category": "operational",
      "severity": 3,
      "score_rationale": "Item 1A bas (frac 0.81), specifique tarifs : 'imposing tariffs on steel and aluminum imports...expanded the scope of their application'. Cout intrants. Citation: \"Important factors affecting our ability to compete successfully include brand and product image, taste and\". Position: bas Item 1A.",
      "trend": "stable",
      "summary": "Sensibilité aux prix de l'aluminium (canettes Midwest premium), sucre, caféine, taurine et aromatisants. Inflation 2021-2023 a comprimé les marges brutes de plusieurs centaines de points, partiellement compensée par hausses tarifaires. Couvertures partielles via achats long terme.",
      "score": 3
    },
    {
      "title": "Acquisitions et risque d'intégration (Bang, alcoholic beverages)",
      "category": "strategic",
      "severity": 2,
      "score_rationale": "Item 1A milieu (frac 0.62), formulation conditionnelle : 'existing operations will be adversely affected as a result of acquisitions'. Bang impairment mentionne. Citation: \"In 2023, we completed our acquisition of the Bang Energy drink business. 2025 Product Introductions\". Position: haut Item 1A.",
      "trend": "stable",
      "summary": "Acquisitions Bang Energy (362 M$, juillet 2023) et CANarchy Craft Brewery (330 M$, 2022, entrée dans bières/seltzers alcoolisés) posent des défis d'intégration et de diversification stratégique. Risque de distraction managériale et de baisse des marges du segment alcool vs energy drinks.",
      "score": 2
    }
  ],
